properties.summary:
backend.rs gives the process one StoreBudget, set once before the first store opens: a shared LRU cache, plus a WriteBufferManager charged to that same cache. Every column family of every store uses the shared cache, with index and filter blocks cached in it, and a 4 MiB write buffer instead of 64 MiB. Every store is capped at 64 open table files.

New `--store-memory <MB>` (default 128) sets the budget. Also new:
- reflow2_core::{set_store_memory_budget, store_memory_usage};
- tools/measure_open_design_memory.py, which splits RssAnon from RssFile;
- a single-test integration binary proving two stores are charged to one budget.
